  "body": "Found while working #885.\n\n**What happens:** `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps` on a 4th axis without TCP (`machine.rtcp` false - e.g. an A that states no tilting direction) resets its modal angle memory `lastA = 0` at every tool change (`onToolChange`) and starts the program at `lastA = 0`. A tilted record at A0 then writes no A word, although the post never commanded A0 and the table may stand anywhere. Reproduced on main (f490458a) with `rotaryBrake: true`:\n\n```\nTOOL 1 T1 / SECTION / Rapid ... A 30000 / Feed ... A 30000 / ENDSECTION\nTOOL 2 T2 / SECTION / Rapid ... A 0     / Feed ... A 0     / ENDSECTION\n```\n\nposts `G00 X0 Y0 Z5 A30` for the first tool, then for the second tool `G00 X0 Y0 Z5` and `G01 X0 Y0 Z0 F100` with no `A0` - the second operation cuts at A30.\n\n**Expected:** the first A of a program, and the first A after anything that may have moved the table, is written; the modal memory is the angle the post last wrote, never an assumed 0. (The G43.4 branch is not affected - its arm writes all three words.)\n\nPR for #885 reads the held angle only from the A words a block actually wrote, so a non-TCP feed that turns from an A the post never placed is now refused by name when the A states a rate - but with no stated rate the wrong program above still posts.\n\nDone means: a pinning test posting the two-tool stream above writes A0 for the second tool (and an opening A0), goldens moved only where an A word was missing, each listed.\n",
